1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,354
Japanese has many sound words, such as kira-kira for sparkling.

2
00:00:09,354 --> 00:00:17,032
They are useful and fun, but they can be hard to remember from a list.

3
00:00:17,032 --> 00:00:26,204
SingLink turns these words into a short quiz and karaoke experience.

4
00:00:26,204 --> 00:00:31,663
First, you choose one of five familiar melodies.

5
00:00:31,663 --> 00:00:37,005
Then you answer four Japanese questions.

6
00:00:37,005 --> 00:00:44,788
After the quiz, Zundamon sings the four correct sentences.

7
00:00:44,788 --> 00:00:54,704
The Japanese lyrics light up with the melody,
and English subtitles explain the meaning.

8
00:00:54,704 --> 00:01:02,924
During OpenAI Build Week, I rebuilt important parts for the Web.

9
00:01:02,924 --> 00:01:15,494
I prepared three hundred and thirty-five learning records with original examples,
meanings, singing readings, and English support.

10
00:01:15,494 --> 00:01:27,544
I also added a responsive English interface, five melody choices,
and timing based on the notes in the score.

11
00:01:27,544 --> 00:01:35,905
Judges can open a fixed demo on GitHub Pages with no setup.

12
00:01:35,905 --> 00:01:43,995
It uses four fixed questions and one pre-generated singing sample.

13
00:01:43,995 --> 00:01:46,947
Normal mode is different.

14
00:01:46,947 --> 00:01:56,210
It chooses four random questions and creates a new song from their correct sentences
on a local Windows computer with VOICEVOX.

15
00:01:56,210 --> 00:02:16,282
I used Codex and GPT five point six to study the old app, move the score logic to the Web,
check the learning data, build the English features, and test the result.

16
00:02:16,282 --> 00:02:24,851
I made the final learning, design, and publishing decisions.

17
00:02:24,851 --> 00:02:34,418
SingLink connects Japanese words, sound, and meaning through karaoke.

18
00:02:34,418 --> 00:02:40,052
It gives learners one more way to repeat and remember.

19
00:02:40,052 --> 00:02:46,517
You can try the public demo from the link on screen.
